-- title:
--   Relative degree is preserved under extension of constants
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $K$ be fields with $K$ a $k$-algebra, and consider the field $k((q))$ of Laurent series over $k$ (the Hahn series field `LaurentSeries k`). Let $E \subseteq E'$ be two intermediate fields of $k \subseteq k((q))$, so both contain the constants $k$, with $E \le E'$, and assume $0 < \mathrm{relfinrank}\, E\, E'$, i.e. the relative degree $[E' : E]$ is finite and nonzero. Let $\mathrm{coeffMap}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ k\ K) : k((q)) \to K((q))$ be the ring homomorphism obtained by applying the structure map $k \to K$ to each coefficient of a Laurent series. Inside $K((q))$ form the intermediate fields $K \cdot E$ and $K \cdot E'$ over $K$, namely the fields $\mathrm{adjoin}$ed to $K$ by the images of the underlying sets of $E$ and of $E'$ under this coefficientwise map. The assertion is the equality of relative degrees
--   $$\mathrm{relfinrank}\,(K \cdot E)\,(K \cdot E') = \mathrm{relfinrank}\, E\, E',$$
--   so in particular $[K \cdot E' : K \cdot E] = [E' : E]$.
--
--   This records the invariance of relative degrees of subfields of a Laurent series field under extension of the constant field, which rests on the linear disjointness of $K$ and $k((q))$ over $k$ inside $K((q))$; the positivity hypothesis restricts the claim to the case of a finite relative degree. It is used in the computation of degrees of fields generated by $q$-expansions of modular functions, where the constant field is enlarged, in [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq) and [`ModularCurve.relfinrank_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_gammaH_inf_gamma0_mul_le_add_one_and_pos`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_gammaH_inf_gamma0_mul_le_add_one_and_pos).
-- source:
